# The rule that makes the devmode terminal worth opening.
#
# NOT READ FROM HERE. sudo only reads /etc/sudoers.d, and this file lives in
# /usr because /usr is the image and /etc is machine-local state that bootc
# three-way merges on upgrade. marwanos-devmode-sudo.service copies it into
# /etc/sudoers.d/50-marwanos-devmode on every boot where
# /var/marwanos/devmode exists, and deletes it on every boot where it does
# not. Shipping it directly in /etc would grant this on machines that never
# asked for it and could never take it back.
#
# WHY IT IS ALL AND NOT A LIST. The terminal exists for the failure nobody
# predicted -- the network that will not come up, the boot that half-worked,
# the unit whose journal is root-only. A curated command list is a guess at
# which emergency will happen, and the emergencies this project has actually
# had (2026-08-08 SSH lockout, 2026-08-10 doors post-mortem) were not on
# anybody's list. On a machine where the flag is set, root over SSH with
# baked-in keys is already open; this is the same door, reachable from the
# sofa instead of from another computer.
#
# NOPASSWD because the player account has no password to type -- it is a
# locked, nologin account that greetd autologins (see 50-marwanos.conf). A
# password prompt here would be an unanswerable question, not a check.
player ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
